__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
# A built wheel, anywhere. `dist/` already covers the ordinary case — `python -m build` writes
# there — but a `pip wheel .` or a `--outdir .` puts one at the repository ROOT, outside every
# rule above, and one sat there untracked across five rounds: `synapse_cdm-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl`,
# one `git add -A` from being committed. Committing a wheel would break
# `tests/test_cdm_packaging.py` and `gates/wheel_install.py`, which compare a BUILT wheel's
# manifest against `git ls-files` in both directions — a tracked wheel makes the artefact part of
# its own input. The rule is the extension and not the one filename, for the reason the archive
# block below gives about itself: a `.whl` is never an artefact this repository tracks, so the rule
# costs nothing and the next stray one does not get to be the test case.
*.whl
.DS_Store

# Documentation site (Docusaurus)
docs/node_modules/
docs/build/
docs/.docusaurus/
docs/.cache-loader/
.wrangler/

# Pinned specification documents. NEVER COMMITTED — and until this block existed that was true
# by discipline plus a test, which is a gate on the COMMIT and not on the operation.
#
# THE FAILURE THIS CLOSES. `tests/test_cdm_pins.py::test_no_pdf_is_tracked_anywhere_in_the_
# repository` asserts `git ls-files` returns no `.pdf` anywhere. It is a good gate and it fires
# after the fact: `git add -A` from the repository root stages all 36 held documents, and only a
# suite run or a reading of `git status` catches it before the commit. That near-miss has happened
# twice. The rule below makes the staging itself refuse, so the gate and the mechanism now fail in
# the same direction and neither is load-bearing alone.
#
# THE EXTENSION SET IS DERIVED, NOT GUESSED. Every file under a `fixtures/*/spec/` directory is a
# `.pdf` (36), a `.json` pin record (6) or a `.py` generator (5), and the last two are exactly the
# committed artefacts — which is why this ignores an EXTENSION and not the `spec/` directory. A
# `spec/` rule would hide the pin records, and the pin record is the whole point of pinning.
*.pdf

# Archives, because that is how a lineage arrives. `cat048_pin.json` records `bundle_url` as
# `https://www.eurocontrol.int/archive_download/all/node/11127` under the link text "Download all"
# — the 22-edition CAT048 lineage came down as one archive. Only `.zip` is evidenced by that
# record; the siblings are listed because they are the same class with the same failure mode and
# none of them is ever an artefact of this repository, so the rule costs nothing and the next
# publisher who serves a tarball does not get to be the test case.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
